🎤 Interview Questions I Learned
What is CloudWatch?

Amazon CloudWatch is an AWS monitoring and observability service used to collect metrics and logs, monitor AWS resources and applications, create alarms, and gain visibility into system performance.

What is a CloudWatch metric?

A metric is a numerical measurement that represents the performance or behavior of a resource or application.

What is a CloudWatch alarm?

A CloudWatch alarm monitors a metric against a configured threshold and can trigger actions when the threshold is breached.

What is CloudWatch Logs?

CloudWatch Logs is used to collect, store, monitor, and analyze log data generated by applications and AWS resources.

CloudWatch vs CloudTrail?

CloudWatch focuses on monitoring and observability, while CloudTrail records AWS API activity and account actions for auditing and governance.